                      #navbar
                        ul
                          li
                            a.g2(href="#link1") 1) Button Click functionality is not working
                          li
                            a.g2(href="#link2") 2) Data is not getting updated
                          li
                            a.g2(href="#link3") 3) How to delete particular data?
                          li
                            a.g2(href="#link4") 4) Icons are not loading..
                          li
                            a.g2(href="#link5") 5) Updated data is not showing in Datatables
                          li
                            a.g2(href="#link6") 6) Unable to open MongoShell
                          li
                            a.g2(href="#link7") 7) Some important MongoShell commands
                          li
                            a.g2(href="#link8") 8) Update operation is not working on "rno" field
                            br
                            br
                            br
                            br
                      .conta.dontshow
                        #link1.gg
                          p Check for errors in click.js folder at Template/public/javascripts/click.js 

                        #link2.gg
                          p a)Check if you missed any ID for that particular field any check the same in index.js folder
                              br
                              |b)Check your database i.e;Monogdb is working in background.if crashed please reinstall the app for concern site and run the app again.
                              br
                              |c)If you're calling an existing fieldname using same ID from anywhere in the code,then such field won't work because an ID should be unique in entire code.
                              br

                        #link3.gg
                          p a)Goto monogdb and apply the following steps
                               br
                               |>use Mob_db  /* It'll switches to database named 'Mob_db' */
                               br
                               |>db.student_data.remove({""})  /* It removes entire collection named 'student_data' */
                               br
                               |Eg: db.student_data.remove{{"rno":"17P31F0011"}}  /* To remove specific data matched with rollno '17P31F0011' */
                        #link4.gg
                          p a)Check your internet connection and refresh the page.Some bootstrap links requires internet connection.
                               br
                               |b)Make sure that indentation is correct in your main code.
                        #link5.gg
                          p Once refresh your home page and check again. If problem still remains restart npm and check again.

                        #link6.gg
                          p If you are unable to open mongoshell i.e;if you try to open mongoshell it forcely closes without mentioning any error.
                          br
                          p Such case arises if the service got stopped in background.
                          br
                          p To solve this problem open task manager>goto services tab>find mongodb>right click on it and click on start.Now reopen the shell and will works fine.
                        #link7.gg
                          p 
                          |1)cls
                          br
                          |To clear the screen
                          br
                          br
                          |2)show dbs
                          br
                          |Displays created database list
                          br
                          br
                          |3)use a
                          br
                          |Creates a database with name a if not exists. If it is an existing db name then it switches to that databases
                          br
                          br
                          |4)show collections
                          br
                          |Displays collections in that database
                          br
                          br
                          |5)db.createCollection('a_coll')
                          br
                          |Creates a collection with name student_data
                          br
                          br
                          |6)db.a_coll.drop()
                          br
                          |Removes a_coll collection from database
                          br
                          br
                          |7)db.a_coll.insert({"name":"gbr","rno":111,"tel":89,"eng":90,"sci":88})
                          br
                          |Adds data with fields in a_coll collection
                          br
                          br
                          |8)db.a_coll.find({}).pretty()
                          br
                          |Displays all data from a_coll in a format
                          br
                          br
                          |9)db.a_coll.find({"name":"gbr"}).pretty()
                          br
                          |Displays records that matched with name as gbr
                          br
                          br
                          |10)db.a_coll.update({"name":"gbr"},{$set:{"tel":95}})
                          br
                          |Updates or Modifies data with field name tel when matches with name gbr

                        #link8.gg
                          p
                          |This application doesn't support updation of RollNo by clicking on update button.
                          br
                          |You have to do this manually from monogdb application
                          br
                          |>db.student_data.update({"sname":"abc"},{$set:{"rno":"17P31F0011"}})
                          br
                          |It'll changes "rno" to "17P31F0011" whose "sname" is matched with "abc" from the collection name "student_data".

